h levels of aged receivables signal collection problems, bad debt exposure, cash flow risk, and potential write-off provisions\u2014all material to council creditworthiness and financial position","iso":"2026-09-08","paper_title":"Appendix D - 2026/27 Aged debt position","paper_url":"https://democracy.eastherts.gov.uk/documents/s74056/74056.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"\u00a3135k additional MRP charge from delayed capital receipts, offset only by temporary investment income benefit","lead":"Delayed capital receipts worsen the council's cash position and the MRP offset is temporary and dependent on interest rates remaining elevated.","iso":"2026-09-08","paper_title":"Financial Management 2026/27 - Quarter 1 forecast to year end","paper_url":"https://democracy.eastherts.gov.uk/documents/s74053/74053.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"52.5% of outstanding debt is aged over 180 days at \u00a30.926m","lead":"High aged debt increases write-off risk and indicates collection challenges that could deteriorate further.","iso":"2026-09-08","paper_title":"Financial Management 2026/27 - Quarter 1 forecast to year end","paper_url":"https://democracy.eastherts.gov.uk/documents/s74053/74053.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Appendix D - 2026/27 Aged debt position","paper_url":"https://democracy.eastherts.gov.uk/documents/s74056/74056.pdf","headline":"52.47% of outstanding debt is aged 180+ days","detail":"As of 30 June 2026, \u00a3925.5m out of \u00a31.76bn total outstanding debt is aged 180+ days. Only 36.35% is current (0-30 days). This concentration of severely aged receivables represents more than half the council's entire debt portfolio and indicates material collection difficulties.","category":"income","matters":"High levels of aged receivables signal collection problems, bad debt exposure, cash flow risk, and potential write-off provisions\u2014all material to council creditworthiness and financial position","figures":"\u00a3925.5m aged 180+ days (52.47% of \u00a31.76bn total); current debt only 36.35%","quote":"Aged Split (%) 36.35% 1.84% 5.70% 2.29% 1.35% 52.47%","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Financial Management 2026/27 - Quarter 1 forecast to year end","paper_url":"https://democracy.eastherts.gov.uk/documents/s74053/74053.pdf","headline":"\u00a3135k additional MRP charge from delayed capital receipts, offset only by temporary investment income benefit","detail":"An additional \u00a3135k Minimum Revenue Provision charge is forecast for 2026/27 because capital receipts anticipated in 2025/26 have been delayed into the current year. This is currently offset by higher investment income from elevated interest rates, but that offset is vulnerable to market changes.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Delayed capital receipts worsen the council's cash position and the MRP offset is temporary and dependent on interest rates remaining elevated.","figures":"\u00a3135k additional MRP charge; offset by higher investment income from current interest rate environment","quote":"an additional \u00a3135K Minimum Revenue Provision (MRP) charge during 2026/27, primarily due to a number of capital receipts originally anticipated in 2025/26 being delayed into the current financial year. This pressure is currently being offset by higher than budgeted investment income, reflecting stronger cash balances and continued elevated interest rates.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Financial Management 2026/27 - Quarter 1 forecast to year end","paper_url":"https://democracy.eastherts.gov.uk/documents/s74053/74053.pdf","headline":"52.5% of outstanding debt is aged over 180 days at \u00a30.926m","detail":"As at end of June, total outstanding debt is \u00a31.764m of which \u00a30.926m is aged greater than 180 days. While this represents a 34% improvement from March 2026, the high proportion of aged debt still signals collection difficulties.","category":"other","matters":"High aged debt increases write-off risk and indicates collection challenges that could deteriorate further.","figures":"\u00a30.926m aged over 180 days (52.5% of \u00a31.764m total)","quote":"Debt aged greater than 180 days is \u00a30.926m, more than half (52.5%) of the total.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Financial Management 2026/27 - Quarter 1 forecast to year end","paper_url":"https://democracy.eastherts.gov.uk/documents/s74053/74053.pdf","headline":"BEAM venue forecasting \u00a3318k income shortfall while using contingency fund","detail":"BEAM is forecasting a net income shortfall of \u00a3318k due to lower than anticipated sales revenue and ongoing fixed operating costs. The council is already deploying \u00a3184k of contingency funding that was specifically established to mitigate in-year financial pressures during the venue's initial years.","category":"income","matters":"A council venue underperforming income targets in its early years, and already consuming contingency, suggests either the business case was over-optimistic or market demand is weaker than planned.","figures":"\u00a3318k income shortfall; \u00a3184k contingency fund deployed","quote":"BEAM is forecasting a net income shortfall of \u00a3318K, primarily due to lower than anticipated sales revenue and the ongoing impact of fixed operating costs. This forecast is after the application of \u00a3184K of contingency funding, which was specifically established to mitigate in-year financial pressures during the venue's initial years of operation.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-08","committee":"Executive","paper_title":"Financial Management 2026/27 - Quarter 1 forecast to year end","paper_url":"https://democracy.eastherts.gov.uk/documents/s74053/74053.pdf","headline":"Planning department \u00a3297k overspend from agency staffing with stated risk of worsening","detail":"Planning is forecasting a \u00a3297k overspend due to continued reliance on agency staff in Development Management caused by recruitment challenges for experienced planning officers. The forecast assumes vacant posts will be filled during the year, but explicitly states: if recruitment proves more difficult than anticipated, the overspend will increase further.","category":"overspend","matters":"This is a controllable cost that has become uncontrollable, and the forecast depends on recruitment success that has not yet been demonstrated. Failure to recruit would push the council further into overspend.","figures":"\u00a3297k planning overspend; recruitment assumptions not yet met","quote":"Should recruitment prove more difficult than anticipated, there is a risk that the overspend will increase further.","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-08"},"name":"East Hertfordshire","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-17","since_iso":"2026-08-18","distress":true,"headline":"52.47% of outstanding debt is aged 180+ days","lead":"High levels of aged receivables signal collection problems, bad debt exposure, cash flow risk, and potential write-off provisions\u2014all material to council creditworthiness and financial position","also":["19 other findings in this window"],"watch":"District Planning Executive Panel on 2026-09-17","n_findings":20,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix D - 2026/27 Aged debt position","top_paper_url":"https://democracy.eastherts.gov.uk/documents/s74056/74056.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":119,"news_drafts_total":3}}